NAME
       group - the local group file

SYNOPSIS
       /etc/group

DESCRIPTION
       /etc/group has one line per local group, readable by everyone, with
       four fields separated by colons:

           NAME:PASSWORD:GID:MEMBERS

       NAME      the group's name.
       PASSWORD  x: a group password, if any, is in /etc/gshadow. Group
                 passwords are rarely used.
       GID       the group ID number.
       MEMBERS   the users who have this group as a SUPPLEMENTARY group,
                 separated by commas. Users whose PRIMARY group it is (the
                 GID field of /etc/passwd) are not listed here, but they
                 belong to it as well.

       Create and change groups with groupadd, groupmod, groupdel, and add
       members with usermod -aG GROUP USER or gpasswd -a USER GROUP. Show a
       group with getent group NAME.

EXAMPLES
           wheel:x:10:student
           admins:x:2000:harry,natasha

           getent group wheel

SEE ALSO
       passwd(5), gshadow(5), groupadd(8), usermod(8), gpasswd(1), vigr(8)
